    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d198">

                <pb facs="0196" n="184" xml:id="pg184"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.00/1938: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-11-07T19:00:00-04:00">November 7, 1942—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5604. Following telegram has been received from Tehran:</p>
                <p>[Here follows text of telegram No. 361, November 6, 5 p.m., from the Minister in
                    Iran, printed on <ref target="#pg179">page 179</ref>.]</p>
                <p>Please urgently advise Foreign Office that we hope British authorities will
                    proceed with utmost caution and regard for Iranian sensibilities in any action
                    which they may take with respect to alleged conspirators. We consider it
                    especially desirable that no public action of any kind be taken against Iranian
                    nationals until tension caused by wheat and currency problems has
                        relaxed.<anchor n="60" xml:id="d198-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d198-f1" n="60" xml:id="d198-f1-content">
                <p>The foregoing paragraph was repeated to the Minister in Iran as Department’s No.
                    311, November 7, 8 p.m., with the following instruction: “In your discretion you
                    may inform British authorities Tehran that above represents Department’s
                    attitude.” (891.00/1937)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
